---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Callout from '../../components/Callout.astro';
import EventStream from '../../components/EventStream.astro';
import PageNext from '../../components/PageNext.astro';
import CtaBlock from '../../components/CtaBlock.astro';
---

<Layout title="Cost accounting — no surprise invoices" pathname="/features/cost">
  <section class="page-head">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="eyebrow-chain">
        <span class="eyebrow">Feature</span>
        <span class="eyebrow-sep">·</span>
        <span class="eyebrow-dim">maddu cost</span>
        <span class="eyebrow-sep">·</span>
        <span class="eyebrow-dim">no provider call</span>
      </div>
      <h1>Cost accounting. <span class="dim-h1">No surprise invoices.</span></h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Catch a runaway session before it's a surprise. Token and call spend rolls up per session, day, runtime, and model — summed from numbers the spine already holds.
      </p>
      <pre class="feat-cli"><code>$ maddu cost --by day
2026-07-05   in 214.8K · out 41.2K · calls 96
2026-07-06   in  88.1K · out 12.9K · calls 37</code></pre>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <header class="section-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">§ 01 · The problem</span>
        <h2>The invoice is the first time you see the spend.</h2>
        <p>
          A single agent session can burn tokens for an hour before anyone notices. By the time the provider's bill arrives, the runaway run is a month old and unattributable. You need the number while it still means something.
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="grid-3">
        <div class="panel">
          <div class="panel-head">
            <span class="panel-title">Roll up any axis</span>
            <span class="panel-aside">local</span>
          </div>
          <p><code>maddu cost</code> aggregates token and call totals per session, day, runtime, and model — read straight from the receipt log and token ledger the spine already keeps. No provider call: it only sums numbers you already have.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="panel">
          <div class="panel-head">
            <span class="panel-title">Set a ceiling</span>
            <span class="panel-aside">opt-in</span>
          </div>
          <p>Drop a <code>.maddu/config/cost-budget.json</code> with <code>windowDays</code>, <code>maxTokens</code>, and <code>metric</code>. Doctor and audit then WARN — never FAIL — when recent spend crosses it, so a runaway is visible before it becomes a bill.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="panel">
          <div class="panel-head">
            <span class="panel-title">Backfill history</span>
            <span class="panel-aside">retroactive</span>
          </div>
          <p><code>maddu import</code> retroactively backfills the ledger from prior runs, so the rollup covers the work you did before you started tracking — not just the sessions since. Old spend becomes accountable too.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <Callout tone="warn" title="A budget warns, it never blocks" tag="cost-budget">
        <p>
          The v1.86.0 cost-budget gate is deliberately WARN-tier. Crossing the ceiling surfaces in doctor and audit as a visible flag, not a failed build — you see the runaway and decide, and the gate never stands between you and a legitimate long session.
        </p>
      </Callout>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <header class="section-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">§ 02 · On the record</span>
        <h2>What a budget crossing looks like on the spine.</h2>
      </header>
      <EventStream
        eyebrow="Cost rollup, ledger to warning"
        source=".maddu/events/2026-07-06.ndjson"
        entries={[
          { time: '15:20:11.003', type: 'TOKEN_USAGE_REPORTED', tone: 'session',   payload: 'in=48120 · out=9204 · model=claude-fable-5',  actor: 'worker-1' },
          { time: '15:20:11.061', type: 'COST_ROLLED_UP',       tone: 'framework', payload: 'by=day · window=7d · total_in=303K',           actor: 'operator' },
          { time: '15:20:11.088', type: 'BUDGET_EVALUATED',     tone: 'accent',    payload: 'metric=tokens · limit=280K · used=303K',       actor: 'doctor' },
          { time: '15:20:11.104', type: 'BUDGET_EXCEEDED',      tone: 'warn',      payload: 'over=23K · tier=warn · build=not-blocked',     actor: 'doctor' },
          { time: '15:21:44.902', type: 'LEDGER_BACKFILLED',    tone: 'ok',        payload: 'source=import · sessions=18 · added=1.2M',     actor: 'operator' },
        ]}
      />
      <p class="feat-note">
        Related verbs: <a href="/capabilities/cost"><code>maddu cost</code></a> · <a href="/capabilities/usage"><code>maddu usage</code></a> · <a href="/capabilities/log"><code>maddu log</code></a> · <a href="/capabilities/import"><code>maddu import</code></a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-narrow">
    <div class="container">
      <a class="btn" href="/docs/features/cost">Read the full reference in the docs <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <PageNext
    eyebrow="Next feature"
    title="Session discipline — never start building unrecorded."
    hint="Hooks auto-register every session and checkpoint governance before every compaction."
    href="/features/discipline"
    tone="accent"
  />
  <CtaBlock />
</Layout>

<style>
  .feat-cli {
    margin: var(--m-space-5) 0 0;
    padding: var(--m-space-4) var(--m-space-5);
    background: var(--m-bg-2);
    border: 1px solid var(--m-line);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--m-accent);
    border-radius: var(--m-radius);
    font-family: var(--m-font-mono);
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--m-fg-1);
    overflow-x: auto;
  }
  .feat-note {
    margin-top: var(--m-space-5);
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--m-fg-2);
  }
  .feat-note code { font-size: 12px; }
</style>
